  "summary": "Hand-tapped Bornean tattoos of scorpions, bunga flowers and spirit animals marking Iban life paths.",
  "description": "Iban pantang tattoos are hammered in with a carved wooden block and mallet-tapped needle — no machine — drawing soot-black bunga terung (eggplant rosette) on shoulders at coming of age, scorpions and crocodiles on thighs, spirit dogs and the hornbill across chests. Each mark narrates: headhunting prowess, river journeys, farming success, protection from spirits. The bunga terung rosette — an eye with fern-spiral petals — remains the core motif from which full chest designs (kalingai) radiate, and revival studios in Kuching keep the tapping tradition alive.",
